Key features and challenges:
-Enhanced protection in NHPs vs either agent alone; 
-Concern over ACAM2000 side effects (myocarditis, eczema vaccinatum); 
-Risk of resistance with tecovirimat.

-Specific and potent inhibition in vitro; 
-Delivery challenges (stability, uptake); 
-Not tested in animals yet.

Recent updates:
-Computational follow-up studies (2024) cite S7M8 as a prototype for dual-pathogen epitope vaccines, suggesting possible adaptation for Mpox–Influenza and Mpox–HIV constructs;
-Subsequent modeling (Fan et al., 2024, Front Immunol) confirms enhanced TLR–ligand coupling stability (>95% confidence) in S7M8’s TLR2 binding domain;
-Part of the growing field of pan-viral synthetic epitope vaccines, integrating TLR-driven immune priming;
-Chinese funding agencies (Beijing Municipal S&T Commission, National Key R&D Program 2022YFA1303500-003) have indicated plans to advance to wet-lab expression.

2024 Publication: 
-Study performed comparative analysis of viral–host gene expression and identified C6R-derived protein K7 as a key target;
-S3I-201 showed highest docking score (≈ -6.5 kcal/mol) and stable binding in 100 ns molecular dynamics simulation (RMSD 0.2 nm);
-Exhibited good ADMET profile (no hepatotoxicity or carcinogenicity);
-Further wet-lab validation recommended for therapeutic potential in Mpox.
